%N A362918 Length of the part of n to the left of the decimal point in the Dekking-van-Loon-canonical base phi representation of n.
%C A362918 a(n) = length of the binary string A362917(n).
%H A362918 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A362918/b362918.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A362918 Michel Dekking and Ad van Loon, <a href="https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers/61-2/dekking04072022.pdf">On the representation of the natural numbers by powers of the golden mean</a>, Fib. Quart. 61:2 (May 2023), 105-118; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.07544">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2111.07544 [math.NT], 2021.
%t A362918 a[n_] := Module[{k = 1}, While[! (LucasL[k] + 1 <= n <= LucasL[k + 1]), k++]; k + 1]; a[0] = a[1] = 1; Array[a, 85, 0] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 12 2026 *)
